{"ts": 1784367012.455162, "event": "finish", "summary": "Held the full 28-frame window. The entry never went meaningfully against the position -- worst dip was -7.5pts at t=4m, a shallow pullback, and price then ran hard to +54-58pts before oscillating down to +24-30pts by the end, still deeply favorable throughout. Never saw a genuine wrong-direction signature (sustained negative excursion with no recovery); the against-fires (KMDR/HA/PROPP) came and went without ever coinciding with the trade actually breaking even or going red, so there was no bail trigger. Next time I'd watch for: px crossing back to negative territory after having been strongly positive, combined with against-fires clustering and low ER10, as the actual wrong-direction tell -- that never happened here.", "exit_frame": null, "n_commits": 29}
